PANEL.md#1:L62:cell:1:s1 [514b8face2]
    `SW_ZERO` pulls the local net `ZEROIZE_SW` low (10k pull-up `R10`, 10 nF `C20`), which the controller reads on GPIO 22; `U12`, a 74LVC1G17 buffer, copies it onto `ZEROIZE_HW` for the ribbons, where the line reaches a test point on B16, a 10k pull-up (`R117`) on A22 and a test point on D8, and no other part listens (decision 30; `gen_sch_c.py:168-178` and `:217` at `45bde541`, corrected 26 September 2026: until `faf8c981` the toggle sat on `ZEROIZE_HW` itself)
    names: refs=C20,D8,R10,R117,SW_ZERO,U12; nets=ZEROIZE_HW,ZEROIZE_SW; boards=A22,B16,D8; gates=buffer,pull-up; gens=gen_sch_c.py:168-178
PANEL.md#1:L63:cell:1:s1 [da6c6735f0]
    `U9` 74LVC1G17 Schmitt-trigger buffer: `EMCON_HW` follows `TX_INHIBIT_n`, both LOW = inhibited (corrected 9 September 2026, red team C1: the part was an inverter and both consumer boards were built on low = silence, so asserting EMCON enabled the PA and released both M.2 radios; a Schmitt input since `faf8c981`, because the toggle's node rises with a 77 us time constant, far outside the 74LVC1G34's input slew limit, `gen_sch_c.py:157-166`).
    names: refs=C1,U9; nets=EMCON_HW,TX_INHIBIT_n; gates=buffer,enabled,inverter,schmitt; gens=gen_sch_c.py:157-166
PANEL.md#1:L63:cell:1:s2 [f4587ac12e]
    Since EQ-25 (stream w4c, 27 September 2026, SC-67) `R14` is 2.2 k 1 % and `R50` (10 k 1 %) holds `TX_INHIBIT_n` down on this board too: with the panel unpowered the line reads 0.24 V under the RF-002 walk's worst-case Ioff sums (1.09 V before), released it rests at 2.57 V (2.37 V at the adverse ends), and it rises with a 17 us time constant.
    names: refs=R14,R50; nets=TX_INHIBIT_n
PANEL.md#1:L63:cell:1:s3 [79b33e8889]
    Since round 8 of MESHSAT-1357 (26 September 2026): the controller reads `EMCON_HW` only through `U13`, a second 74LVC1G17, and `R46` (1k) on GPIO 21, so no firmware pin sits on the line (`feasibility/EMCON.md` item L1); and the hardware EMCON lamp of SD-EMC-6 is drawn: `U14`, a TI SN74LVC1G57 wired as a NOR with Schmitt inputs, reads `TX_INHIBIT_n` and `EMCON_HW` and turns on `Q7` (Si2300DS), which sinks `D22` from `LED_RAIL_SW` through `R47` (470R), so the lamp is lit only while both lines read LOW, with no processor in its path.
    names: refs=D22,L1,Q7,R46,R47,U13,U14; nets=EMCON_HW,LED_RAIL_SW,TX_INHIBIT_n; gates=nor,schmitt
