PANEL.md#5:L147:item:s1 [27d3074deb]
    Boot, in this order: `PI_KILL` driven low (push-pull, and never released while any slot is powered: on the netlist a powered slot's level stage can lift it and switch the kit off, a mechanism not yet measured); `PI_SHDN_REQ` released; the ZEROIZE toggle read (`ZEROIZE_SW`, GPIO 22), and if it is closed, or the flash holds a wipe-pending record, the erase of section 6 is completed before any slot powers; every expander's output register written before its configuration register (the default output register is all ones, so configuration first would switch on the PoE and USB-C stages), keeping `DEV_EN` at 1, which is written 0 only as the last act of a shutdown; the charger's registers written; then the three `SLOT_EN` high, one at a time.
    names: nets=DEV_EN,PI_KILL,PI_SHDN_REQ,ZEROIZE_SW
PANEL.md#5:L148:item:s1 [55d8f49ec8]
    Since board B's round 8 the display switches pass a slot only while that module's own 3.3 V is up (`U519`, `U520` qualify each switch's enable with the slot's power-good, FAB-02), so selecting a dark slot shows no picture rather than feeding the dark module's HDMI pins; with the panel absent B's `R15`/`R16` (10 k) hold both selects low, slot 1.
    names: refs=R15,R16,U519,U520; boards=B's,board B; gates=enable
PANEL.md#5:L149:item:s1 [8d9e44bc9c]
    The PI button: short press = `PI_SHDN_REQ` (clean shutdown of every module), hold 8 s = `PI_KILL`.
    names: nets=PI_KILL,PI_SHDN_REQ
PANEL.md#5:L149:item:s2 [133cca552b]
    The MAIN PWR button is hardware to A22's power controller and the controller only sees its effect.
    names: boards=A22
PANEL.md#6:L155:cell:0:s1 [5e249213b4]
    TX_INHIBIT_n
    names: nets=TX_INHIBIT_n
PANEL.md#6:L155:cell:1:s1 [d306ab46ea]
    `SW_EMCON` closed = low (pull-up `R14` on C7, 2.2k 1 % since EQ-25 and 10k before, 10 nF `C24`, and `R50` (10k 1 %, since EQ-25) down on C7, so the line reads inhibited with the panel unpowered, 0.24 V under the RF-002 walk's worst-case Ioff sums (section 1); A22, B16 and D8 each hold it down with 100k so a cut ribbon inhibits)
    names: refs=C24,C7,D8,R14,R50,SW_EMCON; boards=A22,B16,C7,D8; gates=pull-up
PANEL.md#6:L155:cell:2:s1 [a7e84f7a68]
    D8's KEY gate cannot key the SA868 and the PA (`KEY = PTT_ANY AND TX_INHIBIT_n`); since board A's round 8 candidate (26 September 2026) A22 also reads it, ANDed with `EMCON_HW` into the enables of the PA and HF converters (`U35`, `U37`, SN74AUP1G08, `gen_sch_a.py:1240-1243`), so those two rails do not depend on the firmware pins that reach `EMCON_HW` (`feasibility/EMCON.md` section 4a); the bridge additionally holds every bearer; on C7, with `EMCON_HW`, it lights the EMCON lamp `D22` through `U14` (since round 8)
    names: refs=C7,D22,D8,U14,U35,U37; nets=EMCON_HW,KEY,PTT_ANY,TX_INHIBIT_n; boards=A22,C7,D8,board A; gates=and,enables,gate; gens=gen_sch_a.py:1240-1243
PANEL.md#6:L156:cell:0:s1 [428ab166dc]
    EMCON_HW
    names: nets=EMCON_HW
PANEL.md#6:L156:cell:1:s1 [a3ff8a619c]
    `U9` buffer, low while TX_INHIBIT_n is low; with the ribbon out B16's `R58` (4.7 k 1 percent since board B's round 8; 10k before) and A22's `R102` (10k 1% since board A's round 8 candidate; 100k before) hold it low
    names: refs=R102,R58,U9; nets=TX_INHIBIT_n; boards=A22,B16,board A,board B; gates=buffer
PANEL.md#6:L156:cell:2:s1 [faa935d288]
    as generated at `45bde541` on A22 it is ANDed into the enables of the PA and HF converters (`U26`, `gen_sch_a.py:1102`), and in board A's round 8 candidate it is the second input of `U35` and `U37`, beside `TX_INHIBIT_n` (`gen_sch_a.py:1240-1243`); as generated in board B's round 8 (27 September 2026, MESHSAT-1357), on B16 each single gate `U501` to `U505` (SN74LVC1G08, which state Ioff) ANDs it into the supply enables of the LimeSDR, the RockBLOCK, the LoRa module and both E72, the first three reaching their switches at 0.6 of the gate's output so a gate in its unspecified supply band cannot turn one on (stream w4b), and `U536` ANDs it into the RockBLOCK's own ENABLE (`RB_IEN`, its J3 pin 3), so no firmware holds the module enabled on its capacitors (stream w4b); each slot inverts it into its own `EMCON_ON1..3` in `U112`, `U212`, `U312`, run from that module's own 3.3 V, so a lost `+3V3_DEV` no longer releases a module radio; from there SN74LVC2G06 open-drain outputs pull the module's `WL_nDisable` and `BT_nDisable` low (`U113`, `U213`, `U313`, with the panel's off requests on `U114`, `U214`, `U314`), and `U115`, `U215`, `U315` pull each card's `W_DISABLE1#` low, while each card's supply enable is driven by `U116`, `U216`, `U316` (SN74LV1T08, `EMCON_HW` AND the module's `PCIE_PWR_EN`) from that slot's own 5 V, so all three card supplies go, the 5G module's included, whether or not the module's own 3.3 V is up (stream w4b); the 5G module's `FULL_CARD_POWER_OFF#` falls at once (`U220`) and its socket rail is discharged through 15 Ohm (`Q212`, an AO3400A whose sheet states its threshold and channel resistance at 25 C only, and `R295`), a bound of about 1.2 ms from EMCON to the module's 3.135 V power-off floor plus 1.8 ms per mF of the module's own input capacitance, which no held document states (`feasibility/EMCON.md` section 4b, SD-EMC-1 as re-decided in round 8); the three supervisors read it through the buffer `U506` (`EMCON_SUP`), so no firmware pin sits on the line (`U506` drives `EMCON_SUP` push-pull, so a supervisor its bench jumper leaves unpowered is fed through its PC5 pin, as board C's `U9` fed it before the round); D8's KEY gate makes VHF/APRS the one transmit-only case.
    names: refs=D8,J3,Q212,R295,U112,U113,U114,U115,U116,U212,U213,U214,U215,U216,U220,U26,U312,U313,U314,U315,U316,U35,U37,U501,U505,U506,U536,U9; nets=+3V3_DEV,EMCON_HW,EMCON_ON1,EMCON_ON2,EMCON_ON3,EMCON_SUP,RB_IEN,TX_INHIBIT_n; boards=A22,B16,D8,board A,board B,board C; rails=+3V3_DEV; gates=and,buffer,enable,enabled,enables,gate,inverts,open-drain,supervisor; gens=gen_sch_a.py:1102,gen_sch_a.py:1240-1243
