    Every drive and eMMC key is wrapped by key-encryption keys only B16's ATECC608B holds (two of them, both needed to unlock a drive, `feasibility/ZEROIZE.md` section 3); held closed 5 s, the controller destroys both first over the kit bus by regenerating them in place (the GenKey command), then tells the running modules to drop the keys they hold in RAM, then drops `SLOT_EN1..3`.
    names: nets=SLOT_EN1,SLOT_EN2,SLOT_EN3; boards=B16
