PANEL.md#7:L180:para:s1 [6caaca3cd6]
    Read from the SDA and SCL nets of the committed netlists of boards A, B, C and D at `45bde541`; the 0x48 row from board D's netlist of round 8 (MESHSAT-1357, stream d), whose SDA and SCL gain U22 and nothing else.
    names: refs=U22; boards=board D
PANEL.md#7:L180:para:s2 [94bef6640e]
    **Corrected 26 September 2026 (S-07):** the table listed neither board A's two expanders nor the three supervisors, the Ethernet switch and the PoE controller.
    names: boards=board A
PANEL.md#7:L180:para:s3 [0c8cf23652]
    **An open finding of that correction:** 0x30 is both supervisor 1's status address and the TPS23861's broadcast address, which every TPS23861 answers whatever its A3 pin says, so a transaction the controller means for the supervisor reaches the PoE controller too.
    names: gates=supervisor
PANEL.md#7:L180:para:s4 [108d13c557]
    The broadcast address is fixed in the TPS23861, so it is supervisor 1's address that has to move, in the supervisors' firmware.
    names: gates=supervisor
PANEL.md#7:L180:para:s5 [5b976a9345]
    **Closed 27 September 2026 as a firmware contract (I3-F01, board B round 8, the block `ARCHITECTURE.md` section 5.5 records):** the supervisors answer at 0x34, 0x35 and 0x36; the bus is unchanged, and the panel firmware never writes 0x30 except to address every TPS23861 at once.
    names: boards=board B
PANEL.md#7:L180:para:s6 [ccaf6c5062]
    Three firmware-bearing supervisors share this bus with the secure element; only the panel controller is to command it (firmware rule Z-C3 of `feasibility/ZEROIZE.md`, residual R7).
    names: refs=R7
PANEL.md#7:L182:para:s1 [aedcd950db]
    **Speed, pull-ups and capacitance (27 September 2026, `HW-FW-CONTRACT.md` section 6).** The controller runs the bus in Standard-mode, 100 kHz programmed and at least 90 kHz achieved, the clock `feasibility/ZEROIZE.md`'s time budget holds at (FW-K01).
    names: gates=pull-ups
PANEL.md#7:L182:para:s2 [4ff7998807]
    The pull-ups are 2.2 k on B16 (`R54`, `R55`) and 2.2 k here (`R7`, `R8`), with the KSZ9897R's internal 58 k: 2.94 mA at 0.4 V from the top of the 3.3 V tolerance, against the 3 mA the weakest targets are rated to sink at 0.4 V (the minimum their datasheets state), so they cannot be made stronger, and no participant enables an internal pull-up (FW-K02).
    names: refs=R54,R55,R7,R8; boards=B16; gates=enables,pull-up,pull-ups
PANEL.md#7:L182:para:s3 [385ae55b43]
    Four targets state a 300 ns rise at any clock (the BQ25731, the TPS23861, the ATECC608B and board D's round 8 ADS1115), and as one segment the bus cannot meet it: its pins and ribbons alone exceed the limit at their published maxima (finding HF-F01).
    names: boards=board D
PANEL.md#7:L182:para:s4 [919c0ea875]
    The session took three segments behind two TCA9517A (SC-HF-02): A22's targets and D8's behind one on A22, the three supervisors, the PoE controller and the Ethernet switch behind one on B16 that this controller opens only for its own transactions to them and closes before every secure-element transaction (FW-K05).
    names: refs=D8; boards=A22,B16,D8
PANEL.md#7:L182:para:s5 [b368b57fd0]
    Owed on A22 and B16; until drawn, HF-F01 stands.
    names: boards=A22,B16
PANEL.md#7:L184:para:s1 [0129fb0216]
    The sensor board inside E6 (BME688 at 0x76 and the IMU at 0x68 on its own bus) belongs to the sensor controller, a second RP2040 that is another USB device; its addresses never appear on the kit bus.
    names: boards=E6
PANEL.md#7:L184:para:s2 [c2b91e4453]
    With the ribbon unplugged the kit fails safe on transmit: A22 pulls `EMCON_HW` low (`R102`, as B16 does with `R58`) and A22, B16 and D8 pull `TX_INHIBIT_n` low (`R145`, `R59`, `R2`), so every EMCON gate closes and the PA cannot key; A22 pulls `ZEROIZE_HW` high (`R117`, no wipe) and `SHORE_INHIBIT` low (`R118`, the inputs run).
    names: refs=D8,R102,R117,R118,R145,R2,R58,R59; nets=EMCON_HW,SHORE_INHIBIT,TX_INHIBIT_n,ZEROIZE_HW; boards=A22,B16,D8; gates=gate
PANEL.md#7:L184:para:s3 [1d4232681d]
    The slot enables are pulled low on A22, so no compute module runs.
    names: boards=A22; gates=enables,pulled low
PANEL.md#7:L184:para:s4 [73da5fc77a]
    A kit without its panel neither computes nor transmits, and its charger has no host: at best the pack gains the host-free 256 mA less board E's always-on draw (section 10).
    names: boards=board E
PANEL.md#9:L201:para:s1 [ba3a95b6c7]
    Controls: TEST / ACK short press = acknowledge (flashers to steady, sounder muted, MSG cleared, battery bar 5 s); hold 2 s = lamp test (all seventeen controller-lit indicators for 3 s, a chirp, the battery bar after: the sixteen panel LEDs `D1` to `D16`, the TX lamp `D3` among them through its tie `D17`, and the PI button's ring; the MAIN and TEST rings are lit whenever the LED rail is present and are not the controller's to test, and the controller's status LED `D18` sits on the board, not in the face; reconciled 27 September 2026, S-39: the "17" was right; section 1 counts the face's LEDs, `D1` to `D16` and, since round 8, the hardware EMCON lamp `D22`, which is not among these seventeen: as drawn no expander and no test tie reaches it, so the lamp test cannot light it and setting EMCON is its test, section 4); hold 5 s within 60 s of a "show QR" request from the touch UI = the e-paper shows the enrolment QR while held.
    names: refs=D1,D16,D17,D18,D22,D3
PANEL.md#9:L203:para:s1 [b7ee9bd83e]
    E-paper (PDi E2370KS0C1, 416 x 240, iTC controller, PDi's driving note rev 02): idle page with callsign, battery and shore state, GPS fix, UTC time, last inbound message, bearer chips and the slot health; refresh at most once a minute, full refresh once an hour and after ZEROIZE; the QR carries an enrolment URL plus a one-time code, never key material; the controller powers the display down through `EPD_PWR_n` between refreshes (the boost stage runs only while `BUSY` is high) and polls `BUSY` before every command.
    names: nets=EPD_PWR_n
PANEL.md#9:L205:para:s1 [f6d813396d]
    **SOS indications (S-32's operator half; taken by the session on 27 September 2026 under the owner's standing rule of 26 September 2026, `CONOPS.md` section 7a).** Armed (the toggle closed 2 s): SOS ACTIVE (`D4`) flashes at 1 Hz, MASTER WARN flashes, the sounder runs its SOS pattern, and the e-paper shows "SOS ARMED" with the UTC time.
    names: refs=D4
PANEL.md#9:L205:para:s2 [3e9e9f47d5]
    Sent: `D4` goes steady once the message has been handed to a bearer, the sounder pattern ends, and the e-paper lists each bearer and recipient as the message goes, with the position sent (the LG290P's fix, or the last fix with its age when none is current); MASTER WARN stays until acknowledged.
    names: refs=D4
PANEL.md#9:L205:para:s3 [6e81e4a9e9]
    Queued under EMCON: `D4` keeps flashing, nothing transmits (D-10), and the e-paper shows "SOS QUEUED: EMCON ON, OPEN EMCON TO SEND".
    names: refs=D4
PANEL.md#9:L205:para:s4 [b84bc1b43e]
    No host for the panel (the panel controller's bank without a module, which is bank 1 as board B is generated and bank 3 once board B carries BANK-R1, `CONOPS.md` section 4c; or no module running): the controller shows it by itself, with no bridge: `D4` flashes at 4 Hz, MASTER WARN flashes, and it writes "SOS NOT SENT: NO HOST" on the e-paper.
    names: refs=D4; boards=board B
PANEL.md#9:L205:para:s5 [4f2665c0ff]
    Cancelled (the toggle returned): `D4` goes dark and the e-paper shows "SOS CANCELLED" with the time; a message already sent is followed by a cancellation notice to the same recipients over the same bearers, under the same EMCON rule.
    names: refs=D4
PANEL.md#9:L207:para:s1 [1bc7026f6e]
    Complete (both key-encryption keys destroyed and verified, the journal's DONE record): the sounder sounds continuously for 3 s, MASTER WARN goes steady, and the e-paper is fully refreshed to "ZEROIZED" with the UTC time and "KEYS DESTROYED AND VERIFIED", a page it keeps with the power off; the slots stay off while the toggle stays closed.
    names: gates=and
PANEL.md#10:L213:para:s1 [9e86900b5a]
    `SHORE_INHIBIT` (controller GPIO 20, ribbon pin 26) reaches A22 through B16 and the dock strip E6 through A22's block: high = the shore and vehicle inputs are held off at the front end, so nothing charges.
    names: nets=SHORE_INHIBIT; boards=A22,B16,E6,the dock strip
PANEL.md#10:L213:para:s2 [eb466c8d5a]
    As generated since `458b2873` the charger's cell-count strap is `R26` 13.3k over `R27` 40.2k, 75.1 % of VDDA, inside the BQ25731's 4S window of 68.4 to 81.5 % (ChargeVoltage 16.8 V, SYSOVP and VSYS_MIN at their 4S defaults; TI SLUSE66A 8.5 and Table 9-2; `gen_sch_a.py:764-771` at `45bde541`), and the kit's loads sit on the charger's system node VSYS (the net `VBAT`), with the pack beyond the charge shunt `R17` and the 25 A blade `F1`, TI's own topology (SLUSE66A Figure 10-1; `gen_sch_a.py:18-48`).
    names: refs=F1,R17,R26,R27; nets=VBAT; rails=VBAT,VSYS; gens=gen_sch_a.py:764-771,gen_sch_a.py:18-48
PANEL.md#10:L213:para:s3 [b91071c95b]
    That trickle goes to the pack alone, less board E's always-on draw, which sits on the pack side: a kit with a crashed panel is carried by shore at idle and its pack is held rather than charged (`review-packets/battery/CHARGER-STATE-SEQUENCE.md` sections 2 and 4 to 6).
    names: boards=board E
PANEL.md#10:L213:para:s4 [cba542e37a]
    **Corrected 26 September 2026 (S-07):** this paragraph said the strap selected 2S (`R26` 60.4k) and that the 256 mA fed the loads and the pack together, which was the circuit before `458b2873`.
    names: refs=R26
PANEL.md#10:L213:para:s5 [a9c858ec0a]
    The bridge asks the controller to assert it when the pack temperature (the pack gauge's own thermistor, read by the sensor controller on E6 and reported over USB) is below 0 C, when the operator sets "no charge", and clears it with hysteresis (charge again above 3 C).
    names: boards=E6
PANEL.md#10:L213:para:s6 [bc41670bc5]
    SHORE shows the charger's input-present bit, CHARGING its charge-in-progress bit; the pack is a built 4S smart pack with its own SMBus gauge, read by the sensor controller on E6 (not by the charger), so the battery bar comes from the pack's state of charge as the sensor controller reports it.
    names: boards=E6
PANEL.md#10:L213:para:s7 [f1f111b885]
    As generated since `faf8c981` that path exists: both ends of the pack's SMBus lead are the same JST-XH 1x4 in the pack board's order (1 SMBC, 2 SMBD, 3 the pack's own negative lead, 4 PRES), so a straight four-way lead mates them, and `check_contracts.py` checks the lead as a cross-board contract (ASSEMBLY.md section 4).
    names: boards=the pack board
PANEL.md#10:L213:para:s8 [d1a6b91d38]
    **Corrected 26 September 2026:** this paragraph said E6's end was a 2.54 mm 1x6 header that no lead mated, which was true before `faf8c981`.
    names: boards=E6
CONOPS.md#2a:L107:para:s1 [ad42c9eb94]
    The second pack has no location found yet: no pack is expected to fit the 160 mm west pocket as the board set stands (INFERRED from the committed board B underside, `v2/ecad/tools/panel1450.py` line 23, against the pocket of appendix 32.62; no case measurement is owed since the owner reversed D-08 on 26 September 2026), and the pack ruling D-06 of 26 September 2026 sets one pack in the east pocket, with missions longer than it relying on vehicle or solar input.
    names: boards=board B; gens=panel1450.py
CONOPS.md#2a:L116:cell:2:s1 [82d7099fad]
    `ARCH-PCB-B-IOHA.md` acceptance tests A1 to A14
    names: boards=PCB-B
CONOPS.md#2a:L135:para:s1 [534549e3cc]
    **Which peripherals NEED-03 protects.** Every USB peripheral that `ARCH-PCB-B-IOHA.md` section 15 traces, each designed to move with its bank, and the kit-to-kit WiFi link, whose antennas move to the standby card (IOHA A11).
    names: boards=PCB-B
CONOPS.md#2a:L135:para:s2 [8b09cd80ae]
    The LoRa module (slot 3's SPI) and cellular data (slot 2's PCIe lane), which have no second path and go down with their module, are **NAMED EXCEPTIONS to NEED-03 for prototype 1**, as `ARCH-PCB-B-IOHA.md` sections 15 and 15a and appendix 32.366 record.
    names: boards=PCB-B
CONOPS.md#2a:L135:para:s3 [3118c4d8b8]
    **Settled by the session under the owner's standing rule of 26 September 2026 (SC-02, about 11:35 CEST):** making either bearer critical needs a second LoRa site or the 5G module moved to USB 3, and both change the floor plan of board B, the board that is not routed; the exceptions need no board B change, and without them the kit is designed to keep at least three of D-01's four messaging bearers through the loss of any one module (`ARCH-PCB-B-IOHA.md` section 15a).
    names: boards=PCB-B,board B
CONOPS.md#2a:L135:para:s4 [a3a4d07e30]
    Reverse by naming either bearer critical, which reopens board B's floor plan.
    names: boards=board B
CONOPS.md#M2:L220:para:s1 [782f2efe06]
    **Defined 27 September 2026 (section 4c):** the reduced mode runs two modules, slots 2 and 3, because no single slot can host the owner's example set with the SOS path as board B is generated (Iridium and the panel controller hang on bank 1, whose hosts are slots 1 and 2; the LoRa module is on slot 3's SPI; `ARCH-PCB-B-IOHA.md` sections 4 and 15); it carries GNSS, the LoRa mesh, Iridium, APRS beacons, the SOS path and 5G, with the monitor off.
    names: boards=PCB-B,board B
CONOPS.md#M4:L250:para:s1 [378a24dccc]
    **Must hold:** once EMCON is closed, every transmitter's output falls below the pass line within its row's maximum latency L_max and stays there while EMCON stays closed, by a path that needs no software (NEED-08): 1 s for every radio but the 5G module; for a 5G module that has been turned on, 20 s (REQ-071), where since board B's round 8 the design removes its supply by hardware at once, RF off within about 1.2 ms plus 1.8 ms per mF of the module's input capacitance (TBD, bench E-12), a local reading and not an end-to-end one; 0 at power-up under EMCON (section 4b.1, `feasibility/EMCON.md` section 5a).
    names: boards=board B
CONOPS.md#M4:L250:para:s2 [1922b27e39]
    **Ruled (D-05, 26 September 2026): radios dark.** Every radio with an emission path is powered off or RF-disabled in hardware; the VHF path keeps listening because its gate is on the transmit side only; GNSS, DCF77 and the lightning sensor continue.
    names: gates=gate
