CONOPS.md#4e:L883:cell:0:s1 [b9f6eebae8]
    a device rail lost (`+5V_DEV` or `+3V3_DEV`, one converter each on board A)
    names: nets=+3V3_DEV,+5V_DEV; boards=board A; rails=+3V3_DEV,+5V_DEV
CONOPS.md#4e:L883:cell:1:s1 [a8a12c6168]
    every bank's hub and peripheral is lost; a loss of `+3V3_DEV` releases every EMCON gate hung on `EMCON_ON` or on a slot's `U{s}11` (EMCON.md L3, open under S-01)
    names: refs=L3,U111,U211,U311; nets=+3V3_DEV; rails=+3V3_DEV; gates=gate
CONOPS.md#4e:L884:cell:1:s1 [6c5f98fafe]
    the modules lose each other and the wall port; a module that does not host bank 1 cannot unlock its drives at boot (`feasibility/ZEROIZE.md` R4)
    names: refs=R4
CONOPS.md#4e:L885:cell:1:s1 [e1dfc415de]
    the secure element, the charger, the supervisors' status and board A's expanders are unreachable; drives do not unlock at boot; a wipe that is due cannot be proven, so the slots stay off (fail secure, `feasibility/ZEROIZE.md` section 3.5)
    names: boards=board A
CONOPS.md#4e:L886:cell:1:s1 [e58fe90ad4]
    the mixer fans' tachometers are read by the sensor controller (`gen_sch_e.py` line 503); the cooler fans' are **TBD**; the inside air rises and C1 sheds; on 32.53's still-air figure PS-TYP at +20 C brings the air to about +50 C, where C1 acts (`feasibility/POWER-THERMAL.md` section 9.2)
    names: refs=C1; gens=gen_sch_e.py
CONOPS.md#4e:L886:cell:2:s1 [2cdcdadf40]
    MASTER CAUT "FAN n" for a mixer fan; the C1 indications
    names: refs=C1
CONOPS.md#4e:L887:cell:1:s1 [48a9631e39]
    designed: the bridge shuts every module down, the panel asserts `SHORE_INHIBIT`, and the sensor controller puts the pack in the gauge's shutdown, so the kit is dark and isolated; the threshold is **TBD**, and the path from the sensor to the pack is REQ-042's (the gauge's SMBus shutdown the sensor controller already sends is the one the design has); in the heat stage as board B is generated bank 3 has no host, so the bridge does not learn of it, and what the sensor controller does on its own then is a firmware contract item (**TBD**)
    names: nets=SHORE_INHIBIT; boards=board B
CONOPS.md#4e:L890:cell:1:s1 [cee55e9271]
    the hot stop (section 4c): at +56.5 C, the hottest cell as the gauge reads it, every module shut down cleanly and the switched loads and the charge held off (H1); at +57.0 C the kit shut down by `PI_KILL` (H2); behind it the gauge's OTD and the destructive backstops
    names: nets=PI_KILL
CONOPS.md#4e:L891:cell:1:s1 [b0cc968749]
    the panel controller applies the hot stop's two steps to board B's `TMP117` (+55.0 and +56.0 C) and falls back to the reduced mode with the outlets off; a line shorted to ground reads as H2 and stops the kit
    names: boards=board B
CONOPS.md#4e:L893:cell:0:s1 [67da32c859]
    a permanent pack protection (the second level or the gauge blows F2; the PTC trips)
    names: refs=F2
CONOPS.md#4e:L895:cell:0:s1 [0d119cbc54]
    a push to talk held, or board D's CP2102N RTS line stuck, while the panel controller and the bridge are hung (`feasibility/POWER-THERMAL.md` PWR-F16, round 8, on main since `53a98a71`)
    names: boards=board D
CONOPS.md#4e:L895:cell:1:s1 [a519c88ba6]
    board D's KEY follows the held line in hardware, so the PA stays keyed: K1's 60 s, K2 and C4 are firmware, and nothing in hardware ends the key-down or bounds the flange (PWR-F15)
    names: refs=C4,K1,K2; boards=board D
CONOPS.md#4f:L901:para:s1 [66725c9ccc]
    The heat stage has two columns: its required set, which board B carries once BANK-R1 is in its generator (slot 3), and what board B as generated gives (slot 2), with its shortfall marked (section 4c).
    names: boards=board B
CONOPS.md#4f:L907:cell:5:s1 [af87eaaf24]
    held (dark: its supply removed by hardware at once since board B's round 8, section 4b)
    names: boards=board B
CONOPS.md#4f:L914:cell:1:s1 [4fcc861597]
    the gauge and board P's second level in every mode, PS-SHUT included (the second level destructively, above the cells' limit); past the heat stage, the hot stop on the cells' measured temperature in every mode and on every input state (firmware; HOT-R1 owed on boards A and E, section 4c)
    names: boards=board P,boards A and E
CONOPS.md#5:L920:para:s1 [6fb0e1ba5d]
    **The rule the hardware is designed to:** no transmit serialisation is required; every transmitter may key at once (owner ruling of 4 September 2026, appendix line 2337, restated at line 2465), **bounded since 26 September 2026 by owner ruling D-11**: all at once for a declared key-down time above a declared state of charge, with the outlets at their minimum contract, which is **0 W, the outlets off** (the session's reading of D-11, section 7a; it is what the hardware interlock below does and what `feasibility/POWER-THERMAL.md` assumes).
    names: gates=interlock
CONOPS.md#5:L920:para:s2 [b0cda524e0]
    The session set the thresholds (session choice SC-10 of the requirements registry and the key-down rules K1 to K5 with the in-key guard C4 of `feasibility/POWER-THERMAL.md` sections 7.2 and 9.3), and since 27 September 2026 they are requirement REQ-018's pass lines (the layer-3 closer's session choice on D-11's declared values): every transmitter at once only above a pack rest voltage of 15.5 V, the PA keyed alone only above 12.4 V and never below it (the operator is told); every PA key-down, all-transmit or alone, **at most 60 s** with at least 2 s between key-downs (K1), started only with every cell at most +55 C, the inside air at most +50 C and the PA's flange at most +75 C (K2) and the pack current at most 9.0 A (K3), with the outlets, the pack heater and the standby WiFi card off (K4), and ended early above 18 A, below 2.70 V on any cell or at +85 C on the flange (C4).
    names: refs=C4,K1,K2,K3,K4,K5
CONOPS.md#5:L920:para:s3 [403303aa15]
    Whether the design meets them is feasibility blocker FEA-004's, not an open requirement: the pack chain has to carry its short-time rating at 18 A for 60 s (PWR-F12) and the flange reading has to hold (PWR-F15; the sensor drawn on board D in round 8, on main since `53a98a71`, and read by firmware), and if FEA-004 closes in failure these values reopen; until then one key-down from a +50 C plate is bounded at about 30 s on the record's own figure, and repeated key-downs are OPEN (`feasibility/POWER-THERMAL.md` PWR-F15).
    names: boards=board D
CONOPS.md#5:L920:para:s4 [360270daa1]
    The hardware interlock that drops the outlets while the PA keys, which the design record asks for (32.55 line 2932), is on board A since `458b2873`: `U30` forms OUTLET_OK = NOT (TR_APRS AND PA_EN), low while the PA keys, and two gates of `U26` give POE_EN = POE_SW_EN AND OUTLET_OK and PD_EN = PD_SW_EN AND OUTLET_OK (`gen_sch_a.py` lines 1088 to 1104 at `45bde541`).
    names: refs=U26,U30; nets=OUTLET_OK,PA_EN,PD_EN,PD_SW_EN,POE_EN,POE_SW_EN,TR_APRS; boards=board A; gates=and,gates,interlock; gens=gen_sch_a.py
CONOPS.md#5:L954:cell:4:s1 [79efee6cea]
    **at most 60 s per key-down** (K1), started only inside K2 to K5 and cut by C4 (`feasibility/POWER-THERMAL.md` sections 7.2 and 9.3, PWR-F14); the design record's two figures bracket it: 32.53's "the 200 W peak (PA key-down) lasts minutes" (line 2860) and 32.56's "a 20 s key-down at 45 W" on the plate's local patch (line 2940).
    names: refs=C4,K1,K2,K5
CONOPS.md#5:L955:cell:2:s1 [1007cd40f1]
    plus about 0.9 W for the I/O supervisors (`ARCH-PCB-B-IOHA.md` section 14)
    names: boards=PCB-B
CONOPS.md#5:L973:cell:1:s1 [85c9b8a37f]
    a position beacon every 10 minutes at a fixed site; on the move at most one a minute; each about 1 s, never over K1's 60 s
    names: refs=K1
CONOPS.md#5:L977:cell:1:s1 [73a88e2ff9]
    receive; a transfer transmits in bursts, never with the PA keyed on the pack alone (K4)
    names: refs=K4
CONOPS.md#5:L978:cell:1:s1 [934ca33971]
    a bounded mode: it runs until C1 or C3 ends it
    names: refs=C1,C3
CONOPS.md#5:L979:cell:1:s1 [56a99bef2a]
    off unless the operator enables one; on the pack only inside C2's budget (PWR-F13)
    names: refs=C2; gates=enables
CONOPS.md#5:L986:cell:2:s1 [f5af2c97e9]
    PS-TYP 63.0 W, sustained on the pack while C1 allows it: at +20 C the cells sit at 43.8 to 45.7 C on 32.53's conductance and 45.4 to 81.3 C on the independent bound, so C1 sheds it at +20 C over part of that bound (section 4c)
    names: refs=C1
CONOPS.md#5:L987:cell:2:s1 [51400cfd73]
    PS-TYP plus PoE 100.4 W, plus USB-C 112.3 W, plus both 150.2 W: **bounded, not sustained** on the pack; C2 sheds USB-C then PoE on 9.0 A or a +50 C cell
    names: refs=C2
CONOPS.md#5:L988:cell:2:s1 [526de24db6]
    PS-BUSY, a **bounded mode**: its sustained bound 92.0 W reaches C1's +55 C cell trigger at +20 C on every conductance in the record, so C1 ends it (how long it runs first is **TBD** until the heat capacities are measured)
    names: refs=C1
V2-SPEC.md#MeshSat field kit V2, approved specification (state of 7 Sep 2026, design record sections 32.40 to 32.61):L3:para:s1 [8ca89fa881]
    The 7 September text records the owner's rulings in `MESHSAT-709-geometry-appendix.md` together with proposals the session made under them (the 200 Wh pack of 32.62 was one), and the board generation that implements it is MESHSAT-830 (A22, B16, C7, D8, E6, face plate and case template).
    names: refs=C7,D8; boards=A22,B16,C7,D8,E6
V2-SPEC.md#Case and construction:L9:cell:1:s1 [d2673a4edc]
    3 mm black anodised aluminium plate on the frame's inserts, laser-marked legends and the MeshSat mark; the backer board C7 hangs under it.
    names: refs=C7; boards=C7,the backer
V2-SPEC.md#Case and construction:L9:cell:1:s2 [d45adb955f]
    The plate lies on top of the 1450PF frame over Peli's o-ring, screwed from above into Peli's 6-32 inserts, and the frame stands on four setting legs that give it its height (the session's case choices C1 and C6, `CASE-MARGINS.md` section 4; correction 20)
    names: refs=C1,C6; boards=C6
V2-SPEC.md#Case and construction:L10:cell:1:s1 [e231767e5f]
    twelve gas-discharge arrestors (PolyPhaser GTH-SFF-AL) are the antenna bulkheads, at Z 59 on one 6 mm aluminium RF entry plate per end wall that is also their common ground: east, south to north, 5G MAIN, 5G DIV, the third 5G jack of D-07, IRIDIUM, LORA; west VHF, HF, WIFI 2.4, GNSS, SDR, WIFI P2P A, WIFI P2P B, at a 31 mm pitch (the session's case choices C2 and C4, `CASE-MARGINS.md` section 4; correction 20).
    names: refs=C2,C4
V2-SPEC.md#Case and construction:L10:cell:1:s2 [facb104de6]
    The case generators `panel1450.py` and `case_wall_cutouts.py` carry them since `c351115d`, and the current case set is `release/case-2026-09-27/` (correction 30); the committed boards and the templates of `release/revA/case/` still show the eleven Amphenol 132170 SMA couplers at Z 88 of 32.56 (west VHF, HF, WIFI 2.4, GNSS, SDR; east 5G MAIN, 5G DIV, IRIDIUM, LORA, WIFI P2P A, WIFI P2P B), which is history; every cable ends at the dock strip's float clamp under the stack's blind-mate receptacle (`ecad/tools/panel1450.py` is the single source of the positions and the legends).
    names: boards=the dock strip; gens=panel1450.py,panel1450.py
V2-SPEC.md#Case and construction:L10:cell:1:s3 [5151a2ab87]
    The 5G module's ports are ANT0 to ANT3, not MAIN and DIV: the owner ruled three 5G jacks on ANT0, ANT2 and ANT3, at the board A site found free (X +46), if the case measurement confirms that site and the board E clamp fit, and otherwise two on ANT0 and ANT2 (D-07, 26 Sep 2026; correction 12); the case half is laid out as the east wall's middle arrestor, and the board E clamp fit remains
    names: boards=board A,board E
V2-SPEC.md#Case and construction:L11:cell:1:s1 [e6fa17db79]
    one 114 x 68.3 x 5 mm aluminium connector plate between the hinge fairings, outside the back wall on a closed-cell gasket (the session's case choice C3, `CASE-MARGINS.md` section 4, in place of the 54 x 82 plate between the ribs at X -95 and -18; correction 20): MIL-DTL-38999 shore and USB receptacles (the USB one the Glenair 233-370), sealed Gigabit Ethernet with PoE out, sealed USB-C 45 W outlet (32.57), the M8 receptacle of the outside sensor pod and a ground stud, the stud also taking the two RF entry plates' ground leads.
    names: refs=C3
V2-SPEC.md#Case and construction:L12:cell:1:s1 [c73b56fb81]
    the A22 + D8 + B16 rod stack over the dock strip E6 and block; the 4S pack, built for the kit rather than bought, in the east pocket beside A22 (32.62; one 4S3P block of about 145 Wh by owner ruling D-06, correction 1; the BB-2590/U did not fit and the case stays the 1450); on the lid's inner face the printed tray of the QMX HF unit over the right strip (32.60 item 5) and, over the left strip, a bracket for an 8 to 10 inch rugged tablet (not drawn)
    names: refs=D8; boards=A22,B16,D8,E6,the dock strip
V2-SPEC.md#Case and construction:L13:cell:1:s1 [38a91feb23]
    face plate off (ten 6-32 screws, case choice C1; correction 20), the rod stack lifted straight up off the blind-mate joint without unscrewing a cable, the pack out of its cradle; before the lift the kit is off, the pack's XT60 unplugged and shore removed, and an insulating cap covers the dock block E5 while the stack is out (owner ruling D-14, 26 Sep 2026: lifting live is an accepted, recorded residual risk, and a stack-present interlock is studied at Review D; correction 15)
    names: refs=C1; boards=E5; gates=interlock
V2-SPEC.md#Power:L17:para:s1 [f6633e61d3]
    The node, the inputs, every rail with its part and its EMCON gate: appendix 32.55 (7 Sep 2026).
    names: gates=gate
V2-SPEC.md#Power:L20:cell:1:s1 [306d6f0471]
    one 4S3P block of Samsung INR18650-35E cells, 14.4 V, about 145 Wh (144.7 Wh at the cell's 3,350 mAh minimum), shrink-wrapped in the east pocket under board B with no rigid enclosure, its fit designed against Peli's own figures (owner ruling D-06, 26 Sep 2026, with the D-08 reversal of the same day; `CASE-MARGINS.md`; correction 1).
    names: boards=board B
V2-SPEC.md#Power:L22:cell:1:s1 [cea8161b55]
    14.4 V node; SMBus charger; bucks for 5 V and 3.3 V; 13.8 V rail for the PA stage; the monitor on its own eFuse from the 14.4 V node, the pack heater on its own eFuse and a regulated 12 V buck (corrections 2 and 19); PoE out; USB-C PD out
    names: gates=efuse
V2-SPEC.md#Power:L24:cell:1:s1 [5d18d3f4e9]
    a hardware line from the panel toggle plus a software hold, meant to silence every transmitter (32.50 item 3); on 26 September 2026 the owner ruled that EMCON means radios dark, with the VHF receiver listening behind its transmit-only gate and GNSS, DCF77 and the lightning sensor continuing (D-05).
    names: gates=gate
V2-SPEC.md#Power:L24:cell:1:s2 [c3dc5405b5]
    As generated since `458b2873` the line removes the supply of the SDR, the RockBLOCK, the LoRa module, both E72, the HF unit and the two WiFi link cards, turns off the PA rail, bias and keying while the VHF exciter keeps receiving, pulls the compute modules' own WiFi and Bluetooth disables low through open drains, and puts the 5G module in airplane mode through its disable pin, a mode the module's firmware carries out; since board B's round 8 (27 September 2026) it also removes the 5G module's supply by hardware at once (SD-EMC-1r8, `feasibility/EMCON.md` section 4b; correction 28); read transmitter by transmitter (`feasibility/EMCON.md` section 0a), the radio's own chain closes at desk for 15 of the kit's 17 transmitters and is open for two, the SA868 (its maker publishes no receive threshold for the PTT pin the design holds at 2.677 V or more; bench E-01) and the RockBLOCK 9704 (with its supply cut it runs on its own supercapacitors, about 16 J; its ENABLE is held low by the EMCON hardware since board B's stream w4b, and what the Iridium module does when ENABLE falls is stated in no held document, sections 4.4 and 4c; correction 31), the 5G module's chain closing at desk since board B's round 8; end to end, from the toggle to silence at each antenna port within the latency the session set (1 s, and 20 s for a running 5G module; SD-EMC-7, requirement REQ-071), 0 of 17 rows is closed, every row also waiting on the items the rows share (the toggle and its conductor, accepted by SD-EMC-6 only with a hardware EMCON lamp on board C, drawn since board C's round 8 (`D22`, no processor in its path) with its light guide in the face plate owed (open item S-44), and the line's open items, `feasibility/EMCON.md` sections 3 and 7), and no row has been shown on a bench: feasibility blocker FEA-002 (`CONOPS.md` section 4b; corrections 4, 19, 26, 28 and 30); blackout and NVG panel modes beside it
    names: refs=D22; boards=board B,board C; gates=open drains
V2-SPEC.md#Compute, storage, expansion (B16, about 330 x 200 mm; the distributed fabric of 32.52):L32:cell:1:s1 [bd895a6727]
    **The physical owner is a hardware fabric choice, not a cabling one:** each of the three hub banks is switched between a home module and one neighbour by a 2-of-3 voted selection driven by three I/O supervisors (`ARCH-PCB-B-IOHA.md`), so the loss of one module is meant to move its bank rather than remove it.
    names: boards=PCB-B
V2-SPEC.md#Compute, storage, expansion (B16, about 330 x 200 mm; the distributed fabric of 32.52):L32:cell:1:s2 [13651ca141]
