    names: boards=E4
V2-SPEC.md#Thermal and environment:L73:para:s1 [b89f99d383]
    no vent opening anywhere in the case skin or the plate (owner ruling 7 Sep 2026, 32.53): the heat leaves through the aluminium face plate and the case walls; five IP68-rated internal fans (one per CM5 cooler, two mixer fans under the plate) driven by the sensor controller couple the inside air to the skin; the 30 W PA module bolts flat to the plate's underside on two PEM nuts with a thermal pad (32.56); estimated inside-air rise about 10 K with one module and 16 K with three loaded modules with the lid open (32.53), to be measured by `TEST-PLAN.md` E3; the kit is to be operated shaded, a stated operating condition, with a shade accessory (a lid sun shield or a tarp) and full-sun design a later qualification item (owner ruling D-02e, 26 Sep 2026); with the lid closed the kit runs the reduced mode (owner ruling D-02b of 25 Sep 2026: closed-lid operation in a defined reduced mode, for example GNSS, LoRa mesh, Iridium and APRS beacons, monitor off and one module, with a closed-lid state and thermal test to join `TEST-PLAN.md` and a lid sensor, drawn on board E since `faf8c981` (correction 19); accepted consequences: above +35 C ambient the kit runs one module, and with three loaded modules charging holds off above about +25 C ambient); both restrictions are proposed controls, not established limits: with the current heat budget the design record's own conductance puts the charge hold-off for three typical modules at +19.5 to +21.6 C, the independent bound anywhere from -18 to +19 C, and the hot end is undecided until the enclosure conductance is measured; the design implements the restrictions as controls on the measured pack current and temperatures (the thermal controls C1 to C4 of `feasibility/POWER-THERMAL.md` section 9.3, not the case choices of line 9; the session's choice), and an early heat-balance test is proposed there (finding PWR-F08, feasibility blocker FEA-004; correction 23); the pack's heater mat and the inside climate sensor set the cold-weather behaviour, and a start from a pack cold-soaked below about -10 C at the cells is out of scope for the prototype: it needs shore or vehicle power, or warming, first (owner ruling D-02d, 26 Sep 2026); the case keeps Peli's own pressure equalisation valve (correction 10).
    names: refs=C1,C4; boards=board E
V2-SPEC.md#Open items (the generators have run; these remain owed):L76:para:s1 [d9ae91817c]
    the third 5G jack of the key-B socket (TE 2199119-3 since `458b2873`, whose land carries the maker's two locating holes and whose SIM holders carry the TVS arrays since board B's round 8; corrections 9, 22 and 28), which waits on the board E clamp fit (D-07; its case half is laid out, `CASE-MARGINS.md` section 3.4; correction 12); the KSZ9897, ATECC608B (its full datasheet is under NDA), DS3231, LIS3MDL, TE and Amphenol M.2 drawings (laptop list, 32.54); the sealed USB-C and RJ45 wall parts; the U-174/U headset jacks; the SOS and ZEROIZE cover part; the 2 m antenna; the tablet; the IP68 fans (owner question D-18, open and conditional: it arises only if no 40 mm IP68 fan fits the coolers, and the session then settles it under the owner's standing rule); and, of the design changes the owner's rulings of 26 September 2026 leave to the session, the ones still owed: the RockBLOCK 9704's ENABLE forced low by the EMCON hardware with its stored energy bounded, the SA868's PTT threshold (bench E-01), the hardware EMCON lamp's light guide in the face plate (SD-EMC-6; the lamp is drawn on board C since its round 8, correction 30) and the items every row of the EMCON line shares (D-05, `feasibility/EMCON.md` sections 0a and 7; correction 26; the 5G module's supply removal is drawn since board B's round 8, correction 28), the key-down time and state-of-charge floor as pass lines, PROVISIONAL today (D-11), and the VHF band lock (D-04); in the schematics since `faf8c981`, `458b2873` and `d90f30e4`, and neither laid out nor built: the compute modules' radios and the WiFi link cards' supplies on the EMCON line (D-05), the outlet interlock (D-11), the wall USB data path to the Glenair 233-370 (D-12; correction 13), the pack's secondary protection floor on board P (D-15) and the external ESD array at board A's USB-C CC pins (D-17) (correction 19).
    names: boards=board A,board B,board C,board E,board P; gates=interlock
