    names: boards=board P; gens=gen_sch_p.py
OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#2:L85:cell:2:s1 [916256cba8]
    **-20 to +60 C**, set by its chemical fuse F2 (Eaton SCF9550-30-05); the gauge BQ4050 and the second level BQ7720700 are -40 to +85 C
    names: refs=F2
OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#2:L104:para:s1 [8f59ec89ff]
    The pack's protection is board P; its narrowest part is the chemical fuse F2 at -20 to +60 C, whose top is the cells' own +60 C discharge limit and whose bottom is the envelope's -20 C, so no bound moves.
    names: refs=F2; boards=board P
OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#3:L158:para:s1 [fc58cb90ed]
    **The worst inside air in use**, at the envelope's +40 C with the kit shed to its heat stage (the last stage that keeps a module running; past it the hot stop of section 4 removes every module): in the required stage after BANK-R1, +59.2 C lid open and +62.1 C lid closed on the independent bound's lowest conductance, and +47.8 C and +55.6 C on 32.53's; in the stage board B gives as generated, +57.9 C and +60.6 C, and +47.3 C and +54.6 C (INFERRED: 40 C plus the stage's rise above, rounded down to one decimal).
    names: boards=board B
OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#3:L186:para:s1 [e20bc8f1b4]
    The hold-off is the pack gauge's own: the BQ4050 on board P opens its charge FET outside 0 to 45 C read at the cell surface (`pcb_pack_protection.yaml`, CHARGE_TEMPERATURE_WINDOW), a threshold held in the gauge's data flash rather than fixed in hardware, with the panel's cold-charge inhibit below 0 C on top (`PANEL.md` section 10).
    names: boards=board P
OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#3:L186:para:s2 [31985580ef]
    Decision 40, ruled by the owner on 26 September 2026, adds hardware beside the gauge, and board P's schematic carries it since `faf8c981`: a BQ7720700 second level (cell over-voltage 4.325 V, under-voltage 2.25 V, open wire, and a fixed 70 C over-temperature on its own thermistor since `d90f30e4`) that blows the Eaton SCF9550 chemical fuse F2 once the arming jumper is closed at commissioning, and the gauge's PTC input enabled (`gen_sch_p.py` lines 243, 288 and 414 to 502 at `45bde541`).
    names: refs=F2; boards=board P; gates=enabled; gens=gen_sch_p.py
OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#4:L215:para:s1 [78311d8113]
    2 and 3, monitor off) when its inside air reaches +50 C or any cell +55 C, and, if those are reached again, to one module (the heat stage: slot 3 once board B carries BANK-R1, slot 2 as generated, `CONOPS.md` section 4c); it restores 5 K below (control C1, `feasibility/POWER-THERMAL.md` section 9.3, `CONOPS.md` section 4c).
    names: refs=C1; boards=board B
OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#4:L215:para:s2 [69c53126c9]
    Until 27 September 2026 this line read "above +35 C: the kit runs the reduced mode (one module) so the inside air stays under the +55 C that the battery-bay sensor and the pack need", the figure the owner's D-02b consequence was argued at (section 8), which is not where the current analysis puts it: on 32.53's conductance three typical modules reach C1 at +28.6 to +30.5 C.
    names: refs=C1
OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#4:L215:para:s3 [0a6d39484c]
    What it is for: REQ-077 requires the kit to act before any cell passes +60 C, idle cells on an input included, where the enclosure alone cannot keep them under it, and the design intends the stop to do that once HOT-R1 is in the generators of boards A and E (the requirement reads FAIL on the generated boards until then) and on the provisional error budget (`TEST-PLAN.md` P14); the kit runs no module while it acts.
    names: boards=boards A and E
OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#4:L237:para:s1 [c836951a27]
    At the envelope's -20 C the warm-up holds only while the conductance, lid open with the fans, is at most about 3.6 W/K, which no measurement has shown (T-H1): above it the link cards stay off, the kit-to-kit link is lost at the cold end and `TEST-PLAN.md` E4-O fails on it.
    names: boards=E4
OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#4:L237:para:s2 [84c26222a6]
