OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#4:L285:para:s1 [28447175d0]
    **Operating modes**, each already in the design: full (three modules, lid open), reduced (slots 2 and 3; lid closed, or the measured-temperature and current triggers of `CONOPS.md` section 4c) with its heat stage (one module) and, past it, the hot stop (no module), blackout (LEDs and sounder muted), NVG (panel lighting), EMCON (a hardware line gates every transmitter rail and the PA bias), and charge (mains, vehicle or solar, gated by the pack thermistor and by the cold-charge inhibit).
    names: gates=gated,gates
OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#4:L285:para:s2 [b719e651bd]
    **Corrected 26 September 2026, as generated at `45bde541`:** EMCON removes the supply of the SDR, the Iridium modem, the LoRa, Zigbee and Thread radios, the HF unit, the two WiFi link cards and the PA rail, so those stop receiving too; it pulls the compute modules' own WiFi and Bluetooth disables low in hardware; and it puts the 5G module in airplane mode through its disable pin, a mode the module's firmware carries out; since board B's round 8 (27 September 2026) it also removes the 5G module's supply by hardware at once (SD-EMC-1r8, `feasibility/EMCON.md` section 4b) (`PANEL.md` section 6, `CONOPS.md` section 4b).
    names: boards=board B
OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#4:L285:para:s3 [d23664c78f]
    **D-05, owner ruling of 26 September 2026: under EMCON the radios go DARK.** Every radio with an emission path is powered off or RF-disabled in hardware; the VHF path keeps listening, because its gate is on transmit only; GNSS, DCF77 and the lightning detector continue.
    names: gates=gate
OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#4:L285:para:s4 [e4ba0483d0]
    What is left under that ruling is session engineering: the items every row of the line shares, the SA868's PTT threshold and the RockBLOCK 9704's ENABLE, the 5G module's supply removal being drawn since board B's round 8 (`feasibility/EMCON.md` sections 0a, 5 and 7).
    names: boards=board B
OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#4:L285:para:s5 [c98651fe06]
    The charge gate is the pack gauge's thermistor window (section 3).
    names: gates=gate
OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#4:L302:para:s1 [8f3480949a]
    **Single-fault conditions the design is expected to survive**, written as the design's own protections so that PWR-003 and BAT-002 have something to be judged against: a short on any downstream rail (eFuses), a reversed or over-voltage input (the ideal diode and the 9 to 36 V front end), a shorted pack lead (the 25 A blade and the pack's own protector), a failed module (the voted I/O fabric and the per-bank USB ring), a cell driven past its limits with the gauge's firmware wrong or dead (board P's second level and chemical fuse, decision 40), loss of the panel controller (the hardware EMCON line is independent of any module), and water on the floor of the case (the floor water sensor with pack shutdown).
    names: boards=board P
OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md#4:L302:para:s2 [4acb82ab42]
    **Corrected 26 September 2026:** the loss of the panel controller leaves the transmitters safe but, as generated, no compute module powers without it (`ARCH-PCB-B-IOHA.md` section 10), so it is survived for EMCON and not for compute.
    names: boards=PCB-B
TEST-PLAN.md#MeshSat field kit V2, qualification test plan (MIL-STD-810 and MIL-STD-461 methods; approved 6 Sep 2026, appendix 32.50 item 16e):L3:para:s1 [f1c2c8d45e]
    **Revised 27 September 2026 (MESHSAT-1357, the layer-2 and layer-3 closing actions of the handover audit):** every row now states its **purpose** and the **requirement records it verifies** (identifiers of `v2/ecad/tools/pcb_requirements.yaml`); the stored state keeps the pack fitted (section 1); E5 is written for the sealed case and E8 names Peli's pressure valve; the closed-lid state and its test are defined against the ConOps's reduced mode; D-02a's two pass lines are on every margin; the MIL-STD-461 rows are characterisation (D-04); M7 is at decision 34's ruled level; the thermal characterisation tests the hot end depends on are section 8 and the mechanical fit checks section 9.
    names: boards=E5
TEST-PLAN.md#MeshSat field kit V2, qualification test plan (MIL-STD-810 and MIL-STD-461 methods; approved 6 Sep 2026, appendix 32.50 item 16e):L3:para:s2 [5f30437813]
    **Pass 2, later on 27 September 2026, answering the first pass of Review A (`reviews/REVIEW-A-LAYER-2-2026-09-27-pass1.md`):** E3-L carries E3-A's whole pass line with the lid closed, requires the owner's D-02b example set with the SOS path at every level (the generated board's shortfall is not waived), and fails on an SGP41 above +55 C (findings B4 and B5); E4-O restores round 8's +1.0 C charge floor and -9.0 C discharge stop and requires the kit-to-kit link after the cold warm-up (B7, m10); T-H3 replaces `ASSEMBLY.md`'s ten-minute key-down (B6); the transport and stored states have every input unplugged (m5).
    names: boards=A's,E4
TEST-PLAN.md#MeshSat field kit V2, qualification test plan (MIL-STD-810 and MIL-STD-461 methods; approved 6 Sep 2026, appendix 32.50 item 16e):L3:para:s3 [b9f3eb411b]
    **The second release attempt of layers 1 to 3, later on 27 September 2026 (the release checks' layer 2 B2 and layer 3 R4):** P15 (section 7) forces the hot stop at room temperature on the pack and on shore, so REQ-077 is verifiable whatever a chamber reaches; E3-H gains a stepped run beyond the envelope and the rule that a step that acted in no run reads NOT_VERIFIED; E3-L's pass line is unchanged.
    names: refs=R4
