ASSEMBLY.md#4:L180:para:s1 [ea68c64a4d]
    Twelve Preci-Dip 813 contacts in `J_DOCK` on A22's underside land on the raised block's targets: pins 1 to 4 carry `VIN_RAW` (the 9 to 36 V input and the solar tracker's output, passed up to A22's front end), 5 to 7 ground, 8 `SHORE_INHIBIT`, 9 and 10 the USB pair of E6's sensor controller, 11 ground and 12 a spare (`gen_sch_a.py:225`, `gen_sch_e.py:488`; corrected 26 September 2026, S-07: this sentence put the wall outlet's console pair on 9 and 10).
    names: refs=J_DOCK; nets=SHORE_INHIBIT,VIN_RAW; boards=A22,E6; rails=VIN_RAW; gens=gen_sch_a.py:225,gen_sch_e.py:488
ASSEMBLY.md#8:L204:item:s1 [f2fbb5a56a]
    A22 alone, pack not connected: a bench supply at 14.4 V on the node contacts through a 5 A limit.
    names: boards=A22
ASSEMBLY.md#8:L204:item:s2 [ebf7b76ff6]
    With `EMCON_HW` low the PA and HF rails stay off (corrected 26 September 2026: this read "high"; the line is active low, `PA_EN = EMCON_HW AND PA_SW_EN` in `gen_sch_a.py:535-536`, and `R102` pulls it low (`:537`) with the ribbon out, so on a bare A22 the two rails stay off until the line is driven high).
    names: refs=R102; nets=EMCON_HW,PA_EN,PA_SW_EN; boards=A22; gates=and; gens=gen_sch_a.py:535-536
ASSEMBLY.md#8:L206:item:s1 [dc6e921095]
    The stack with B16: each module boots from its rail with the other two slots disabled, then all three together; every USB device enumerates on its hub; the Ethernet switch links all three and the wall port.
    names: boards=B16
ASSEMBLY.md#8:L208:item:s1 [b023a2e379]
    Panel: the panel controller enumerates; lamp test lights all seventeen controller-lit indicators (the sixteen panel LEDs `D1` to `D16`, the TX lamp `D3` among them through its tie `D17`, and the PI button's ring; `PANEL.md` section 9); BLACKOUT kills the rail; the EMCON toggle locked closed keeps the SA868 and the PA in receive while the bridge asserts PTT and opens every transmitter rail gate, and every other radio goes dark (D-05, `PANEL.md` section 6), measured with an external receiver; ZEROIZE armed shows on the e-paper and, held 5 s, performs the erase of `PANEL.md` section 6 (decision 30: the secure element's wrapping key destroyed, the running modules' RAM keys dropped, the slots cut), after which no drive unlocks; SOS closed 2 s under EMCON queues its message and tells the operator (D-10, `PANEL.md` section 9).
    names: refs=D1,D16,D17,D3; gates=gate
ASSEMBLY.md#8:L210:item:s1 [7857aaa69d]
    Shore inhibit: `SHORE_INHIBIT` high holds the front end off within a second, low restores it.
    names: nets=SHORE_INHIBIT
ASSEMBLY.md#8:L211:item:s1 [0a98178adb]
    PA: key-downs of at most 60 s each at 30 W into a load, at least 2 s apart, each started only inside K2 and ended by C4 (`feasibility/POWER-THERMAL.md` sections 7.2 and 9.3), as `TEST-PLAN.md` T-H3 runs them; the flange sensor and a thermocouple beside it logged, and the case skin temperature recorded, the fans running.
    names: refs=C4,K2
ASSEMBLY.md#8:L211:item:s2 [c3f8dd9765]
    **Corrected 27 September 2026 (Review A of layer 2, finding B6; `CONOPS.md` section 4d):** this step was ten minutes of key-down at 30 W, which K1 forbids: one 60 s key-down at 45 W of heat from a +50 C plate already puts the flange at about 95 C on the record's own figure, against the RA30H1317M1's +100 C case maximum and its 90 C advice (PWR-F15).
    names: refs=K1
ASSEMBLY.md#8:L212:item:s1 [1b157a50d3]
    Blind-mate: lift the stack and set it back three times, each time by the procedure of section 7 (kit off, outside leads and pack unplugged, the cap on E5 while it is out).
    names: boards=E5
ASSEMBLY.md#8:L213:item:s1 [857ee4d62b]
    Pack gauge data flash (decision 40, owner ruling of 26 September 2026), before the pack is first charged or discharged: read the BQ4050's protection thresholds and enabled protections back and compare them with `pcb_pack_protection.yaml`.
    names: gates=enabled
ASSEMBLY.md#8:L213:item:s2 [42ab04ebc5]
    Board P's second level covers cell under-voltage in hardware since `faf8c981` (D-15's first branch), so the read-back is the check D-15 keeps; only after it passes is the chemical fuse armed by closing `JP1` (`gen_sch_p.py` docstring and `:476`; corrected 26 September 2026, S-07).
    names: refs=JP1; boards=P's; gens=gen_sch_p.py
ASSEMBLY.md#9:L217:item:s1 [c54e91925e]
    A22: the Preci-Dip 813-S1-012-10-016101 spring connector and the nine Mill-Max 0858 class power pins on the underside (tails soldered on the top face), the eleven Radiall R222M00720 blind-mate receptacles, the Keystone 3568 holder with its 25 A mini blade, the inductors that have no assembler equivalent (read the ORDER-NOTES), the rail leads, the PA, HF, monitor and heater leads, the MAIN button lead, the wall USB-C leads.
    names: boards=A22
ASSEMBLY.md#9:L218:item:s1 [3fa744781d]
    B16: the three Compute Modules (CM5108064) on their receptacles and standoffs, the three coolers with their fan leads, the WiFi link card, the 5G module with its two SIMs, the three NVMe drives, the LimeSDR, the RockBLOCK on its bracket, the CR2032, the rail and PoE leads from A22, the antenna pigtails, the HDMI cable, the camera and QMX leads, the panel and A-B ribbons; the LG290P, the E22 and the two E72 are assembled where JLCPCB stocks them, else hand-soldered.
    names: boards=A22,B16
ASSEMBLY.md#9:L219:item:s1 [dcfe5ddc9a]
    C7 (the backer under the plate; the switches, the jacks, the camera and the sounder mount in the plate and only their leads reach the board): the sixteen 3 mm LEDs standing on the top face under the light guides (beaded to 5.3 mm), the Floyd Bell sounder with its gasket, the three C&K switches, the NKK toggle, the three APEM toggles with their covers, the two U-174/U jacks, the camera module, the PDi e-paper on its ZIF, the RP2040 and its flash if JLCPCB has no stock, the two XH leads.
    names: refs=C7; boards=C7,the backer
ASSEMBLY.md#9:L220:item:s1 [18bf292849]
    D8: the SA868 module where JLCPCB has no stock, the G6K relay if short, the U.FL and SMA leads to the PA and the antenna, the two headset pigtails, the VGG lead; the PA module itself is a plate part.
    names: refs=D8; boards=D8
ASSEMBLY.md#9:L221:item:s1 [7211912728]
    E6: the three Keystone holders with their blades, the JST-VH DC and solar leads, the XT60 counterpart and the SMBus socket (JST-XH 1x4), the lid and tamper reed on `J_TAMP`, the twelve signal wires and the 12 AWG pair up to the block, the printed float clamp bar (`v2/cad/float_clamp.py`: one part, twelve 8.5 mm cavities, 22 M3 x 8 into the strip's clamp holes at the mid-pitch points between cavities, each plug's cable laid in its own slot to the south or north and tied through the bar's two tie slots beside it) with their Radiall R222M80500 plugs, the DCF77, Geiger and lightning modules on standoffs beside the strip, the two mixer fans, the water strips, four VHB pads.
    names: refs=J_TAMP; boards=E6
ASSEMBLY.md#9:L222:item:s1 [c648bf2ea2]
    P1 (inside the pack): the 25 A blade in F1, the four 2.5 mm2 solder lands (the block's B+ and B- straps, the pack's two 12 AWG leads), the five tap wires into J_CELL, the four cell thermistors into J_TS and the second level's own thermistor into J_TS2 (on the hottest cell), the SMBus lead into J_SMB; the gauge's golden image from bqStudio over the SMBus before the lid goes on, and the arming jumper JP1 left open until section 8 step 12 (corrected 26 September 2026, S-07).
    names: refs=F1,JP1,J_CELL,J_SMB,J_TS,J_TS2
