pcb_decisions.yaml#40:L896:field:outcome:s1 [4698174d5f]
    THE FLOOR, which is the session's engineering and stands under either branch: a 4S secondary over-voltage protector across the four taps, a chemical fuse in the pack path that the secondary protector AND the BQ4050's own FUSE output (its pin 25) can both blow, and the BQ4050's PTC input turned on instead of tied off.
    names: gates=and
pcb_decisions.yaml#40:L896:field:outcome:s2 [a89adf0d12]
    If a 4S secondary protector that also covers under-voltage can be sourced near the cost of the over-voltage-only part, it is used; otherwise the under-voltage protection stays in the BQ4050's firmware and the residual is accepted, with a verification of the gauge's data flash (the thresholds and the enabled protections read back against `pcb_pack_protection.yaml`) as a commissioning step.
    names: gates=enabled
pcb_decisions.yaml#40:L896:field:outcome:s3 [4f6b62b753]
    IN BOARD P'S SCHEMATIC SINCE faf8c981 (round 4 of MESHSAT-1357), with the second level's over-temperature network of d90f30e4: a TI BQ7720700 second level (3S to 7S; cell over-voltage 4.325 V, cell under-voltage 2.25 V, open wire, and a fixed 70 C over-temperature on its own 103AT-2 thermistor; SLUSEG7D, v2/vendor/battery/ti-bq77207.pdf) whose COUT and the BQ4050's FUSE output both drive the heater switch of an Eaton SCF9550-30-05 chemical fuse F2 through the arming jumper JP1, which is closed at commissioning after the gauge's image is written and read back; its DOUT holds the discharge FET off below 2.25 V; and the BQ4050's PTC input is enabled with a Murata PRF15BB103RB6RC chip PTC element (gen_sch_p.py:243, :288 and :414-502 at 45bde541).
    names: refs=F2,JP1; gates=enabled; gens=gen_sch_p.py:243, :288 and :414-502
pcb_decisions.yaml#40:L896:field:outcome:s4 [c1269c680b]
    It is not laid out: the committed board P layout (P4) predates the schematic and is re-placed and re-routed at board P's next phase, and BAT-001 on board P stays open until that copper exists and pack_protection judges board P as generated (S-45).
    names: boards=P4,board P
pcb_decisions.yaml#40:L896:field:reversed_by:s1 [b7bc3415b2]
    reopen this decision and take the second level, the chemical fuse and the PTC element out of board P's schematic (gen_sch_p.py), which carries them since faf8c981; no board P layout carries them yet
    names: boards=board P; gens=gen_sch_p.py

